A||||6||dragnlo||Heater Core Removal||||1||
Z||000000||dragnlo||05-10-2000||02:55 PM||||Has anyone replaced there heater core. I was wondering about how long it took and if the dash has to be pulled. It doesnt look like it needs to come out but I havent started yet either  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||87PegasusGT||05-10-2000||03:18 PM||||Good news. I am so little mechanically inclined, I can just barely change my own oil, and it took me about 40 minutes  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> All you have to do is pull the speaker, and remove 3 or 4 screws and pop the new core in. The hardest part will be pulling the hoses off in the front. I recommend pulling or at least moving the coolant reservoir.||||reg||1
Z||000002||wkayl||05-10-2000||03:21 PM||||I changed the one on mine with A/C and factory sub-woofer.  Drain coolant, unhook heater hoses, remove sub-woofer box, remove cover on heater housing, remove core.  reverse to reinstall.  It took me about an hour.   ||||reg||1
Z||000003||dragnlo||05-10-2000||04:22 PM||||Thanks I ordered it today and it will be here tommorrow, I guess I am going to do it tommorrow now that I know the dash doesnt have to come out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Thanks again<BR>Dorian||||reg||1
Z||000004||WKDFIRO||05-10-2000||10:25 PM||||You don't have to drain the coolant. First time I did it I forgot, but it wasn't bad, spilled some but then the core will be full too. Taking off the speaker? I didn't do that either. But if that helped thats the key. I think you meant the Window washer resevoir, not the coolant resevoir. Then you can get to the heater hoses.||||reg||6
Z||000005||Fiasco||05-10-2000||11:13 PM||||Hah! One of the few times I'm glad I don't have AC is when I have to change my heater core. The whole thing can be done from the spare tire compartment in like 20 minutes.<BR>I moved the washer tank, disconnected a few wires and the heater hoses, and removed the 7 or 8 screws holding the blower motor housing. Then there's one more screw on the bracket which holds the core itself. ||||reg||10
Z||000006||dragnlo||05-11-2000||08:26 PM||||I just wanted to thank everyone that replied, I got it done today, it took about 1.5 hours, it took me longer to get the hoses off then to drain and take apart a/C and put it all back together. Thanks again, dragnlo<P>SO nice not to smell antifreeze  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
